1057851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EldritchMinister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1043792-pugmire-fillable-pdf?p=1057691#post1057691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awesome! This will work nicely in my Roll20 games. Unfortunately no one has designed one yet for their system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was working on one actually. Guess I'll just turn lazy and wait now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12984-harp0","name":"Harp0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12984_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T16:09:45-07:00","id":1106308,"title":"","content":"I'd like to bump this up - Is there a tabletop simulator that uses the Pugmire character sheet as of yet? Or have people been using the Fillable pdf on roll 20?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T08:35:12-07:00","id":1106575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eddyfate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1043792-pugmire-fillable-pdf?p=1045706#post1045706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once the PDF is finalized after the errata phase, we'll offer a fillable PDF (want to make sure there are no errors on the character sheet first).</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there an ETA on this of curiosity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T07:38:02-07:00","id":1108395,"title":"","content":"Bumping this - I''m really wanting to start up an online Pugmire game, but there are a lack of tools to do so :I, especially without fillable character sheets/online sheets<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T02:20:47-07:00","id":1108669,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the delay -- I was in the middle of a complex and chaotic move from the US to Ireland, so I didn't see your comments until today. No need to bump in future -- I do read everything when I'm able. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> We do plan to work with Roll20 to produce Pugmire-specific resources. A lot of that was waiting on the book being printed first, but now that it's done, I believe Onyx Path is starting that conversation with Roll20. I don't have an ETA on when Roll20 will be done, though -- a lot of it is on their timetable.<br /> <br /> As for the fillable PDF character sheet, it'll be available with the Pugmire PDF and PoD via DriveThruRPG. That will go on sale once Kickstarter backers start getting their shipments, so probably in a manner of weeks.<br /> <br /> I'm glad everyone's excited, and I know it feels like Pugmire has been around forever, but in truth we're really only getting started. Tools are things we're wanting to support, but we want to make sure they're done well, which will take some time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15-eddyfate","name":"eddyfate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T06:11:21-07:00","id":1109203,"title":"","content":"How about getting Pugmire added to Hero Lab?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T13:09:29-07:00","id":1109363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eddyfate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1043792-pugmire-fillable-pdf?p=1108669#post1108669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for the delay -- I was in the middle of a complex and chaotic move from the US to Ireland, so I didn't see your comments until today. No need to bump in future -- I do read everything when I'm able. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> We do plan to work with Roll20 to produce Pugmire-specific resources. A lot of that was waiting on the book being printed first, but now that it's done, I believe Onyx Path is starting that conversation with Roll20. I don't have an ETA on when Roll20 will be done, though -- a lot of it is on their timetable.<br /> <br /> As for the fillable PDF character sheet, it'll be available with the Pugmire PDF and PoD via DriveThruRPG. That will go on sale once Kickstarter backers start getting their shipments, so probably in a manner of weeks.<br /> <br /> I'm glad everyone's excited, and I know it feels like Pugmire has been around forever, but in truth we're really only getting started. Tools are things we're wanting to support, but we want to make sure they're done well, which will take some time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hey Eddy - glad to hear your move went well <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Sorry, It had been sometime and a lack of official response was disheartening. Currently I've done some light changes of html on a custom sheet for a D&amp;D 5E sheet (since its so very similar). I am excitedly looking forward to Pugmire and have been already creating homebrew content for other factions like the badgers, lizards and other kooky concepts like primates which proclaim they are the true heirs to the Code of Man, proclaiming they even possess Man's blood &amp; DNA. I find Pugmire has so much potential for Light RP and I'm eagerly looking forward to the full release.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T13:10:22-07:00","id":1109366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>karpomatic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cav